From 0075d356ba519bdf2af80843b30db71e71725c4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:52:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Verifier V26: single-lot records, canonical addresses,
 contradictions, lowered CONSUMED [skip ci]

- Single-lot records: OpenLot, SetLotQuota, SetLotOrder, RevokeLotOrder
  and ConsumeLot are matched against the record each logs
  (LOT_OPENED, LOT_QUOTA, LOT_ORDER with the grantee's tag from its
  Citizen, LOT_REVOKED with what the kernel released, LOT_CONSUMED),
  and no LOT_LOSS on the lot. A full match now needs the record; one
  not shown is UNVERIFIABLE (CloseLot's CLOSE is not compared).
- Contradictions: two records of one kind and key for one instruction
  are a FAIL even when one of them matches (the program logs one).
- Addresses: a lot or vault the replay reads must be at its own address
  (addr::lot / addr::vault, public create_with_seed derivations), a
  single-lot instruction's vault the lot's vault, OpenLot's lot the new
  lot's address, a ship order's and a deposit's vault at theirs, as the
  program checks. Before, the same states at another account replayed
  to a match.
- History: a CONSUMED that falls between two recorded states (a return
  of unused goods, which no record kind shows yet) is UNVERIFIABLE,
  CustodyHistoryUnexplained. Before, it produced no V26 finding at all.

No rule, ABI number, record kind or version changes. Tests (no key
generated, derived or used to sign): the single-lot cases with their
records, each record byte changed, missing, shown twice, a stray loss;
lots and vaults at other accounts (single-lot and caravan); another
standing vault at its own address; a lowered CONSUMED alone and after a
use; through verify() with the records as Program data lines, a
SetLotQuota with its record is a full match and without it is not.

